   "report": "<h3>About this data</h3>\n<p>These videos are previews rendered by OriginFlow: the egocentric camera with per-finger force traces (left and right hand),\na hand-pose overlay, head and wrist trajectories, and an annotation timeline (episode, subtask, atomic action). The raw\nstreams are not part of this folder, so the viewer shows the renders as delivered, downsampled from 120 to 30 fps.</p>\n<h3>Data quality, as reported by the provider</h3>\n<p>Frame-level validity flags over the OriginData preview dataset (10,867,077 frames). They count valid or detected frames;\nthey do not measure force or pose accuracy.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th><th class=\"num\">Rate</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>left.force_valid</td><td>Left-hand force values valid</td><td class=\"num\">99.84%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>right.force_valid</td><td>Right-hand force values valid</td><td class=\"num\">99.84%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>observation.hand.left.detected</td><td>Left hand detected</td><td class=\"num\">93.24%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>observation.hand.right.detected</td><td>Right hand detected</td><td class=\"num\">96.09%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>observation.head.pose_valid</td><td>Head pose finite and aligned (not tracking quality)</td><td class=\"num\">100.00%</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3>Real-robot training results, as reported by the provider</h3>\n<p>Eight tasks trained from scratch (starVLA with a DiT-B head, batch 32; 641 sequences over 10 tasks, 525 train / 116 test):\nafter 20,000 post-training steps the mean success rate was 34.35% with force input and 28.30% without. Squeezing salad\ndressing with 50,000 pretraining and 10,000 post-training steps: 75% (15/20) with force, 55% (11/20) without. Gains vary\nby task; stamping went from 15% without force to 10% with it.</p>\n<div class=\"figs\"><figure><img src=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/yxma/human-mcap-viewer-media/resolve/main/media/of/fig/post-training-efficiency.png\" alt=\"Overall real-robot success rate across eight tasks at different post-training step counts.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Overall real-robot success rate across eight tasks at different post-training step counts.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/yxma/human-mcap-viewer-media/resolve/main/media/of/fig/pretraining-scale-benefits.png\" alt=\"Squeezing salad dressing: pretraining scale, with post-training fixed at 10,000 steps.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Squeezing salad dressing: pretraining scale, with post-training fixed at 10,000 steps.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/yxma/human-mcap-viewer-media/resolve/main/media/of/fig/pretraining-comparison.png\" alt=\"Squeezing salad dressing with and without pretraining.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Squeezing salad dressing with and without pretraining.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/yxma/human-mcap-viewer-media/resolve/main/media/of/fig/real-robot-task-summary.png\" alt=\"Success rates and confidence intervals for eight tasks after 20,000 post-training steps.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Success rates and confidence intervals for eight tasks after 20,000 post-training steps.</figcaption></figure></div>"
